Ladybird drops empty ordinary declarations, and retains
empty custom properties. Blink routes ordinary declarations
through CSSPropertyParser::ParseValueStart(), WebKit uses
CSSPropertyParser::parseValue() with consumers such as consumeQuotes(),
and Gecko dispatches from PropertyDeclaration::parse_into()
to the property grammar.

Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 rejected empty
display and quotes values even with whitespace, comments or !important.
WebKit accepted an empty list-style shorthand. Ladybird follows Chrome
and Firefox for that case.
